      "side": 1,
      "message": "Skia doesn\u0027t make multiple IBs in practice (or use IB arrays for that matter) so I didn\u0027t think it was necessary to support them. We would need to name each uniform struct and then look up the name when emitting variable-reference prefixes. Because I know I only support one, I can simplify things by hard-coding the name prefix as `_uniforms.`. I believe SPIR-V also limits itself to one IB only:\n\n```\n// We can only have one interface block (because we use push_constant and that is limited\n// to one per program)\n```\n\nI\u0027ll need to look at how SSBOs are handled, that might complicate things. I haven\u0027t looked too closely at those yet.",
